---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="FOMC minutes, June 17, 2026 | The Catch" current="Records">
  <div slot="locator" class="locator"><span>RECORD</span><span>June 17, 2026</span></div>
  <div class="content">
    <main class="record-page">
      <p class="record-kicker"><a href="/events/fed-rate/">&larr; The federal funds rate</a></p>
      <h1>The minutes: unanimous on the hold, split on what comes next</h1>
      <p class="record-sub">Minutes of the June 17, 2026 FOMC meeting, released July 8, 2026. They record who voted, and the case a few participants made for a hike.</p>

      <div class="excerpt">
        <p class="excerpt-label">From the minutes</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>&ldquo;In their consideration of monetary policy at this meeting, all participants supported
          maintaining the current target range for the federal funds rate. &hellip; A few participants commented
          that, in light of these developments, there was a case for raising the target range for the federal
          funds rate, but those participants indicated that they supported maintaining the current target range
          at this meeting. Several participants remarked that they did not see the current policy stance as
          restrictive.&rdquo;</p>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote>
          <p>&ldquo;Voting for this action: Kevin Warsh, John C. Williams, Michael S. Barr, Michelle W. Bowman,
          Lisa D. Cook, Beth M. Hammack, Philip N. Jefferson, Neel Kashkari, Lorie K. Logan, Anna Paulson,
          Jerome H. Powell, and Christopher J. Waller. Voting against this action: None.&rdquo;</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="excerpt-source">Full text: <a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomcminutes20260617.htm" rel="noreferrer">federalreserve.gov</a></p>
      </div>

      <p class="record-note">
        What this record is: the Committee's own account of its June discussion, published three weeks after
        the decision. It shows the hike case forming behind a unanimous vote; at the next meeting, July 29,
        three of these voters dissented in favor of an increase. The decision-day record is the companion
        <a href="/claims/fomc-statement-june-17-2026-rate-range-maintained/">statement</a>; the full analysis
        is on the <a href="/events/fed-rate/june-2026/">event page</a>.
      </p>

      <details class="how-checked">
        <summary>How we checked this</summary>
        <p>The quotes above were captured directly from the Federal Reserve's website and compared word-for-word
        against the published minutes. The source page was saved at capture time so the record stays verifiable
        even if the page changes. Details of our process are on the <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a>.</p>
      </details>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .record-page { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
  .record-kicker { font-family: "Public Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 0.8rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .record-kicker a { color: #5b6470; text-decoration: none; }
  .record-kicker a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .record-page h1 { font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; text-wrap: balance; }
  .record-sub { font-family: "Public Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; color: #5b6470; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .excerpt { border: 1px solid #e3e0da; border-left: 3px solid #2e7d5b; background: #fbfaf8; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; }
  .excerpt-label { font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace; font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #22604a; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .excerpt blockquote { margin: 0 0 0.9rem; }
  .excerpt blockquote:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .excerpt blockquote p { font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .excerpt-source { font-family: "Public Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 0.8rem; color: #5b6470; margin: 0.75rem 0 0; }
  .record-note { font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .how-checked { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .how-checked summary { font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace; font-size: 0.8rem; color: #5b6470; cursor: pointer; }
  .how-checked p { font-family: "Public Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #454c55; background: #f6f5f2; padding: 0.8rem 1rem; border-radius: 3px; margin: 0.5rem 0 0; }
</style>
